{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9cba96db-ba61-4c84-9bee-005a30d53911","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the issue, fixed [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-uZhMeF/run-vibe.sh), and documented the root cause in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-uZhMeF/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n\n* **Root Cause**: \n  During startup, Mistral Vibe attempts to query credentials from the macOS Keychain by spawning `/usr/bin/security`. However, [agent.sb](file:///tmp/h-uZhMeF/agent.sb#L10) explicitly denies executing `/usr/bin/security` (`(deny process-exec ... (literal \"/usr/bin/security\"))`). The sandbox blocks the process with `[Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`, terminating Vibe with exit code 2 before it executes the prompt.\n* **Fix**:\n  Set `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` in the allowlisted environment within [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-uZhMeF/run-vibe.sh#L14-L15). This instructs Vibe's keyring subsystems to bypass OS keyring/Keychain resolution entirely and rely directly on `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.\n","duration_seconds":337.341027,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":251184,"output_tokens":7639,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":2278773,"total_tokens":258823}}}
